.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pr 1  "pr " 
.SH NAME
pr \- Work with pull requests (`checkout` fetches the head branch)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpr\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Work with pull requests (`checkout` fetches the head branch)
.PP
`ifg pr create` defaults `\-\-head` to the current branch and refuses to open a PR whose commits are not pushed yet. `checkout` fetches the PR head — from the fork when the PR came from one — into a local branch named `pr\-<number>`; running it again fast\-forwards that branch, and it falls back to the server\*(Aqs `refs/pull/<n>/head` mirror when the head branch has been deleted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pr\-list(1)
List pull requests
.TP
pr\-view(1)
Show one pull request
.TP
pr\-diff(1)
Print the diff of a pull request
.TP
pr\-create(1)
Create a pull request (head defaults to the current branch)
.TP
pr\-merge(1)
Merge a pull request
.TP
pr\-review(1)
Review a pull request
.TP
pr\-checkout(1)
Fetch the PR head branch and check it out as pr\-<number>
.TP
pr\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
